(P/'README-landing-page.md').write_text('''# Francesco Ferri — GitHub Pages landing page

## Install
Copy `index.html`, `cv.html` and the `assets` folder into the root of `ffrancesco/ffrancesco.github.io`, replacing the existing index.html. Commit the change to the branch used by GitHub Pages. Keep all existing lectures, reveal.js, custom, main.js and CNAME files.

No build step, dependencies, tracking or external fonts are needed. Open index.html locally to preview. The six published lecture links use absolute URLs, so they also work from the local preview.

## Add another course or lecture
Edit index.html. Each course is a clearly grouped `<details class="course">` block. Add lecture rows using the existing `<div class="lesson">` pattern. Replace the unpublished-materials text with real links when available. Use the exact case of each filename. Print-view URLs are Reveal.js pages, not pre-generated PDFs.

## CV and content notes
The editable online CV is cv.html. The PDF is assets/Francesco_Ferri_CV.pdf. The supplied build_ferri.py regenerates this package and the PDF (requires Python and ReportLab; update its output folder and font paths for your machine).

Employment and education dates follow the uploaded Ferri_Resume.pdf, including Associate Professor from 2022 and the overlapping Campania role. The current institutional email, office phone and ORCID follow AAU VBN. Languages are listed without inferred proficiency. The research assistant institution was absent in the supplied CV and has not been invented. The private telephone number, personal email and referee's contact details are omitted from this public-facing version.

Teaching descriptions reflect the courses discussed with Francesco; only the six links listed on the existing homepage are presented as published materials. Other repository files, including revised lecture versions, have not been substituted silently.

Selected publications were checked against VBN on 28 September 2026. This is a selected list, not a complete bibliography. VBN has inconsistent issue metadata for some articles, so the affected entries use journal, volume and article number without an issue. No citation counts are included.

Sources: https://vbn.aau.dk/en/persons/ffer/ and the individual publication links in cv.html; existing homepage https://ffrancesco.github.io/; supplied Ferri_Resume.pdf.
''')
